So the AMENDED conjecture ALLOWS many forms in the window (3/38 k=2, 4/51 k=3, ...).
(G) is STRONGER: NONE of these is ACHIEVED by a real 12-speed family. Key question: is k
BOUNDED for achievers? Fan-Sun: n=4 has k in {1,2} only; exceptions are generalized APs.

Fan-Sun counterexample structure (generalized APs), for reference:
  n=4: ML(8,4r+3,4r+11,4r+19)=(2r+7)/(4(2r+7)+2), k=2  [value 7/30 at r=0, ABOVE 2/9 -- 2nd gap]
  n=6: ML(5,6,11,17,23,28)=8/51 ; n=7: ML(1,3,4,5,7,13,18)=3/23
  n=6 {5,6,11,17,23,28}: M_exact=8/51 (paper claims 8/51) match=True
  n=7 {1,3,4,5,7,13,18}: M_exact=3/23 (paper claims 3/23) match=True
